course: dictionary
lesson: 7663
title: Proofreading your work
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To proofread means to read your writing slowly and carefully to find and fix mistakes in spelling, punctuation and grammar. It is the last check before your work is handed in or printed.
explain: Proofreading looks for small slips, not big changes. «Editing means improving the writing, while proofreading means hunting the small slips.» So a stronger word or a missing sentence is editing, but a missing full stop or a wrong spelling is proofreading.
explain: Read slowly, one line at a time, because your eyes skip over mistakes when you read fast. Reading your work aloud helps, and so does reading one sentence at a time from the end, so you see each word on its own.
fact: To proofread means to read carefully to find and correct mistakes.
fact: Proofreading is the last step of the writing process: plan, draft, revise, edit, proofread.
fact: Proofreading checks spelling, punctuation and grammar, such as capital letters, full stops and verb tenses.
fact: A proofreader is a person whose job is to check writing for mistakes before it is finished or printed.
fact: Proofreading marks are short signs that show where a correction should go on a printed page.
exercise: Mia wrote «i went to the park.» What should she do when she proofreads? | *Fix the capital letter at the start of the sentence | Add a whole new paragraph about the park | Give the story a new title | Change the story to a different place
exercise: Which step of writing comes last? | *Proofread | Plan | Revise | Draft
exercise: «She goes to school yesterday.» What should a proofreader spot here? | The word school is spelt wrong | The title is too long | *The verb tense does not match yesterday, so it should be went | The sentence needs a new character
test: Which job is a proofreading job? | *Finding a missing comma in a sentence | Choosing a better word to describe the setting | Rewriting the ending of the story | Moving the middle paragraph to the start
test: What does proofread mean? | To write a story from start to finish | To read quickly to get to the end | *To read carefully to find and correct mistakes in spelling, punctuation and grammar | To print a book on a machine
exam: In the writing process, which three steps come in this order at the end? | *Revise, edit, proofread | Edit, proofread, revise | Proofread, edit, revise | Draft, revise, proofread
